            </section>

            <section class="prose-section" id="honest-nuances">
                <h2>The honest nuances</h2>
                <p>Offline does not mean &ldquo;can never leave your device,&rdquo; and it would be dishonest to imply otherwise.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>System backups can include app data.</strong> Android backup and Apple-managed backups are platform services, not WeekScale sync. Whether they run depends on your device and backup settings.</li>
                    <li><strong>Export is real and user initiated.</strong> When you export, the file leaves the app and the destination's privacy practices apply.</li>
                    <li><strong>No cloud restore.</strong> Because there is no server, there is nothing to restore from &mdash; which is exactly why backups and exports matter.</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="guide-principle">
                    <strong>Offline is a boundary, not a magic promise.</strong>
                    <span>WeekScale keeps the boundary strong; what you do with your own data is up to you.</span>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="prose-section" id="tradeoffs">
                <h2>The tradeoffs of no account, no cloud</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>There is no password to reset and no vendor account to recover.</li>
                    <li>There is also no WeekScale server that can restore history after data loss.</li>
                    <li>Automatic multi-device synchronization is not available.</li>
                    <li>Backups and CSV copies are your responsibility.</li>
                    <li>Support cannot inspect or repair a private database remotely.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>Those constraints are deliberate. They reduce convenience in exchange for a much smaller data footprint and a far simpler trust model. If that trade is exactly what you are looking for, WeekScale is built around it.</p>
            </section>

